 "capsule": "Minamoto no Yoritomo established Japan's first warrior government at Kamakura after crushing the Taira clan at the Battle of Dan-no-ura in 1185, receiving the title of shogun from the emperor in 1192 while the imperial court remained a ceremonial fixture in Kyoto. After Yoritomo's death in 1199 real power passed to his widow's family, the Hojo, who ruled as hereditary regents (shikken) over a succession of largely powerless Minamoto, Fujiwara, and princely shoguns. The shogunate survived the Jokyu War of 1221 and repelled two Mongol invasion fleets in 1274 and 1281, but the fiscal strain of those campaigns fed the unrest that let Emperor Go-Daigo topple the Hojo regency in the Kenmu Restoration of 1333.",
